# clang-tidy profile for fork-authored lakehouse C code.
#
# Scope: only files authored by this fork (see specs/lakehouse/RULES.md §3 —
# upstream and core-allowlist files keep upstream formatting untouched).
#
# Checks omitted deliberately because they fight PostgreSQL coding
# conventions (single statements unbraced, short loop identifiers are
# idiomatic upstream):
#   readability-braces-around-statements, readability-identifier-length,
#   readability-magic-numbers, readability-function-cognitive-complexity
# insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: memcpy is the idiom across
#   the PostgreSQL tree; buffer lengths are validated at each call site.
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: strong-typed params would deviate
#   from the FFI surface defined by cbindgen output.
#
# Run via scripts/run_clang_tidy_lakehouse.sh (needs a built tree for
# compile_commands + generated headers).
---
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  performance-*,
  readability-duplicate-include,
  modernize-macro-to-enum
HeaderFilterRegex: src/backend/access/lakehouse/.*
